  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kvinna till Kvinna EU accession and Women&#xb4;s Rights Western Balkans 2020-2026 - KtK EU accession and Women&#xb4;s Rights Western Balkans 2020-2026, ny strategi</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kvinna till Kvinna EU-n&#xe4;rmande och kvinnors r&#xe4;ttigheter V&#xe4;stra Balkan 2020-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intended impact: 

Womens rights are increasingly respected and equal participation
in decision-making takes place in the Western Balkans

Programme outcomes:

1. Kvinna till Kvinna and Women&apos;s Civil Society Organisations (WCSOs) have strengthened engagement on gender equality with European Union (EU), member states, United Nations (UN), and other national stakeholders

2. Kvinna till Kvinna and targeted WCSOs have built new alliances and strengthened existing ones to promote gender equality in Western
Balkans.

3. Targeted WCSOs have the capacity to conduct effective advocacy.

Assumptions:

Western Balkan Governments and parliaments
&#x2022; continue to be committed to the EU accession processes;
&#x2022; realise the necessity to promote, respect and implement laws and policies
relevant for womens rights and womens participation and influence, and to
persecute any violations of such legislation;
&#x2022; commit to upholding the rule of law.

EU and other international stakeholders
&#x2022; uphold their own commitments andde clared principles regarding realising
gender equality and protecting womensrights and womens participation;
&#x2022; uphold their own commitments and declared principles regarding priorities in the pre-accession process of the Western Balkan countries; and
&#x2022; insist on adherence/fulfilment of the requirements of the acquis.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Programmet syftar till att st&#xe4;rka kvinnors r&#xe4;ttigheter och lika deltagande i beslutsfattande i v&#xe4;stra Balkan, att bidra till att integrera j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet i EU-n&#xe4;rmandeprocessen samt att st&#xe4;rka kvinnor&#xe4;ttsr&#xf6;relsen i de sex f&#xf6;rmedlemskapsl&#xe4;nderna. Programmet fokuserar p&#xe5; p&#xe5;verkansarbete gentemot EU:s institutioner. F&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsteorin g&#xe5;r ut p&#xe5; att om EU lever upp till sina &#xe5;taganden om m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet kommer det att p&#xe5;verka regeringar och parlament i v&#xe4;stra Balkan-regionen s&#xe5; att de stiftar och genomf&#xf6;r lagar och policys som &#xe4;r relevanta f&#xf6;r kvinnors r&#xe4;ttigheter och lika deltagande. Programmet st&#xf6;djer femton lokala organisaitoner i regionen som tillsammans bedriver p&#xe5;verkansarbete b&#xe5;de p&#xe5; nationell niv&#xe5; och p&#xe5; EU-niv&#xe5;.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program aims to continue to strengthen women&apos;s rights and women&apos;s equal participation in decision-making in the Western Balkan region, and to contribute to gendering the EU accession processes and strengthening civil society organisations the six pre-accession countries. Focus in the program implementation is put on advocacy towards EU institutions. The theory of change is that if EU upholds its commitments to human rights and gender equality it will have a direct influence on the Western Balkan governments and parliaments to legislate for and implement laws and policies relevant for women&#x2019;s rights and women&#x2019;s equal participation. The program provides financial support and capacity building to 15 strategic partner organisations in the region to join and effectively influence policy discussions at national level, at the EU level and in other international fora.</narrative>
  </description>
